Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Act is to secure the financial resources necessary to strengthen the competitiveness of agriculture and fisheries, expand industrial infrastructure in agricultural and fishing villages, and implement development projects in agricultural and fishing regions.
[Wholly amended 2010.12.30]

Article 2 (Definitions)
(1) "Reduction or exemption" in this Act means any of the following cases in which income tax, corporate tax, customs duties, acquisition tax, or registration and license tax on registration is not imposed or is reduced under the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, Customs Act, Local Tax Act, or Restriction of Special Local Taxation Act. <Amended 2010.12.30, 2021.12.21, 2024.12.31>
1. Non-taxation, exemption from tax, reduction of tax, tax credit, or income deduction;
2. Application of the special corporate tax rate to cooperative corporations and other corporations under Article 72(1) of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, or application of the special income tax rate to interest income or dividend income under Articles 89(1) and 89-3 of that Act;
3. Application of the special acquisition tax rate under Article 15(1) of the Local Tax Act.
(2) "Principal tax" in this Act means the following. <Amended 2001.12.29, 2005.1.5, 2007.12.31, 2010.3.31, 2010.12.30>
1. For special rural development tax under Article 5(1)1, the relevant income tax, corporate tax, customs duties, acquisition tax, or registration and license tax on registration that is reduced or exempted;
2. For special rural development tax under Article 5(1)2, income tax;
3. Deleted. <2010.12.30>
4. For special rural development tax under Article 5(1)4, individual consumption tax;
5. For special rural development tax under Article 5(1)5, securities transaction tax;
6. For special rural development tax under Article 5(1)6, acquisition tax;
7. For special rural development tax under Article 5(1)7, leisure tax;
8. For special rural development tax under Article 5(1)8, comprehensive real estate holding tax.
(3) Terms other than those defined in paragraphs (1) and (2) have the meanings prescribed by the Acts governing the principal taxes. <Amended 2010.12.30>
[Title amended 2010.12.30]

Article 3 (Persons Liable to Pay Tax)
A person falling under any of the following subparagraphs is liable to pay special rural development tax under this Act. <Amended 1994.12.22, 1998.12.28, 1999.12.3, 2001.12.29, 2005.1.5, 2007.12.31, 2010.1.1, 2010.3.31, 2010.12.30, 2021.12.21>
1. A person granted reduction of or exemption from income tax, corporate tax, customs duties, acquisition tax, or registration and license tax on registration under the Acts specified in the portion of Article 2(1) preceding its subparagraphs;
2. Deleted. <2010.12.30>
3. A person liable to pay individual consumption tax on goods specified in Article 1(2)1(a) and (b) and Article 1(2)2(b)1) and 2) of the Individual Consumption Tax Act among the goods under Article 1(2) of that Act, or on admission under Article 1(3)4 of that Act;
4. A person liable to pay securities transaction tax under Article 3(1) of the Securities Transaction Tax Act;
5. A person liable to pay acquisition tax or leisure tax under the Local Tax Act;
6. A person liable to pay comprehensive real estate holding tax under the Comprehensive Real Estate Holding Tax Act.
[Title amended 2010.12.30]

Article 4 (Non-Taxation)
Special rural development tax shall not be imposed in any of the following cases. <Amended 1994.12.22, 1995.12.29, 1996.10.2, 1997.8.30, 1997.12.13, 1998.2.24, 1998.9.16, 1998.12.28, 1999.2.5, 1999.12.28, 2000.10.21, 2000.12.29, 2004.7.26, 2009.3.18, 2009.4.1, 2010.3.31, 2010.12.30, 2011.12.31, 2014.1.1, 2014.5.14, 2014.12.31, 2015.6.22, 2015.12.15, 2016.12.20, 2018.12.31, 2019.12.31, 2021.12.21, 2022.12.31, 2023.12.31, 2024.12.31, 2026.1.27, 2026.4.21, 2026.5.12>
1. Reduction or exemption granted to the State (including a foreign government), a local government, or a local government association;
2. Reduction or exemption prescribed by Presidential Decree granted to farmers or fishers (meaning farmers under Article 3(2) of the Framework Act on Agriculture, Rural Community and Food Industry and fishers under Article 3(3) of the Framework Act on Fisheries and Fishing Villages Development; the same applies hereinafter), or organizations whose members are farmers or fishers (including agricultural partnership corporations, agricultural business corporations, and fisheries partnership corporations under the Act on Fostering and Supporting Agricultural and Fisheries Business Entities);
3. Tax reduction or exemption, or special tax reduction or exemption, for small and medium enterprises under Articles 6 and 7 of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act;
3-2. Reduction of or exemption from capital gains tax under Articles 40, 91-26, and 91-27(1) and (2) of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act;
3-3. Reduction or exemption resulting from income deduction under Article 16 of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act;
4. Reduction or exemption for savings, interest income, or dividend income under Articles 86-3, 86-4, 87, 87-2, 87-5, 88-2, 88-4, 88-5, 91-14, 91-16 through 91-22, 91-25, and 91-28 of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act;
4-2. Reduction of or exemption from acquisition tax under Article 58-3(1)1 and (2)1 of the Restriction of Special Local Taxation Act;
4-3. Reduction of or exemption from registration and license tax under Article 58-3(3) of the Restriction of Special Local Taxation Act;
5. Reduction or exemption for nonresidents or foreign corporations among reductions or exemptions for interest income and other income under Article 21 of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act;
6. Reduction of or exemption from customs duties under international conventions, international practice, or the like, as prescribed by Presidential Decree;
7. Cases where securities transaction tax is not imposed under Article 6 of the Securities Transaction Tax Act or a zero tax rate applies under Article 8(2) of that Act: Provided, this excludes cases where a zero tax rate applies to the transfer value of securities transferred on a securities market prescribed by Presidential Decree among securities markets under the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act;
7-2. Cases falling under Article 117(1) and (2) of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act;
8. Reduction of or exemption from acquisition tax and registration and license tax prescribed by Presidential Decree for formal acquisition of ownership, registration or recording of a mere change in description, acquisition of temporary buildings, substitute acquisition due to natural disasters, and the like, under the Local Tax Act and the Restriction of Special Local Taxation Act;
8-2. Deleted. <2014.12.31>
9. Reduction of or exemption from acquisition tax or registration and license tax on registration for modest housing prescribed by Presidential Decree;
10. Acquisition tax on farmland and forest land to which Article 6(1) of the Restriction of Special Local Taxation Act applies;
10-2. Acquisition tax on motor vehicles under Article 124 of the Local Tax Act;
10-3. Reduction of or exemption from registration and license tax under Article 35(1) of the Restriction of Special Local Taxation Act;
10-4. Acquisition tax under Article 15(1)1 through 3 of the Local Tax Act;
10-5. Acquisition tax under Article 8(4) of the Restriction of Special Local Taxation Act;
11. Acquisition tax on modest housing and farmhouses prescribed by Presidential Decree;
11-2. Reduction or exemption under Articles 20, 100, 140, and 141 of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act;
11-3. Reduction or exemption under Articles 30-2 and 30-4 of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act;
11-4. Reduction or exemption under Article 121-24 of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act;
12. Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree in which non-taxation of special rural development tax is deemed necessary to secure national competitiveness or ensure efficient operation of the national economy, including technology and human resources development, asset formation by low-income persons, and public-interest projects.
[Title amended 2010.12.30]

Article 5 (Tax Base and Tax Rates)
(1) The amount of special rural development tax is the amount calculated by multiplying the tax base in each of the following subparagraphs by the corresponding tax rate. <Amended 1994.12.22, 1998.12.28, 1999.12.28, 2000.12.29, 2001.12.29, 2005.1.5, 2007.12.31, 2010.12.30, 2013.5.28, 2021.12.21, 2024.12.31>

| No. | Tax base | Tax rate |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | Amount of reduction of or exemption from income tax, corporate tax, customs duties, acquisition tax, or registration and license tax on registration under the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, Customs Act, Local Tax Act, and Restriction of Special Local Taxation Act (excluding the case in subparagraph 2) | 20/100 |
| 2 | Amount of reduction of or exemption from income tax on interest income or dividend income under the Restriction of Special Taxation Act | 10/100 |
| 3 | Deleted. <2010.12.30> | |
| 4 | Individual consumption tax payable under the Individual Consumption Tax Act | |
| 4(a) | Cases under Article 1(3)4 of the Individual Consumption Tax Act | 30/100 |
| 4(b) | Cases other than item (a) | 10/100 |
| 5 | Transfer value of securities traded on securities markets prescribed by Presidential Decree among securities markets under the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act | 15/10,000 |
| 6 | Acquisition tax calculated under the Local Tax Act, Restriction of Special Local Taxation Act, and Restriction of Special Taxation Act by applying 2/100 as the standard tax rates under Articles 11 and 12 of the Local Tax Act | 10/100 |
| 7 | Leisure tax payable under the Local Tax Act | 20/100 |
| 8 | Comprehensive real estate holding tax payable under the Comprehensive Real Estate Holding Tax Act | 20/100 |

(2) For cooperative corporations and other corporations under Article 72(1) of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, paragraph (1)1 applies by treating the amount obtained by subtracting the tax amount in subparagraph 2 from the tax amount in subparagraph 1 as the amount of tax reduced or exempted. <Amended 2010.12.30>
1. Corporate tax calculated by applying the tax rates under Article 55(1) of the Corporate Tax Act to the corporation's tax base for each business year;
2. Corporate tax calculated by applying the tax rates under Article 72(1) of the Restriction of Special Taxation Act to the corporation's tax base for each business year.
(3) In cases of non-taxation or income deduction, paragraph (1)1 applies by treating the amount calculated by the method prescribed by Presidential Decree as the amount of tax reduced or exempted. <Amended 2010.12.30>
(4) Where income tax on interest income or dividend income is not imposed, or special income tax rates apply, under the Restriction of Special Taxation Act, paragraph (1)2 applies by treating the amount obtained by subtracting the tax amount in subparagraph 2 from the tax amount in subparagraph 1 as the amount of tax reduced or exempted. <Amended 2010.12.30, 2021.12.21, 2024.12.31>
1. The amount calculated by multiplying interest income and dividend income by the following rates:
(a) For interest income, 14/100;
(b) For dividend income, 14/100;
(c) Deleted. <2024.12.31>
2. Income tax payable under the Restriction of Special Taxation Act (zero where income tax is not imposed).
(5) Notwithstanding paragraph (1)6, in cases falling under Article 15(2) of the Local Tax Act, acquisition tax calculated under that paragraph is deemed the tax base under paragraph (1)6. <Newly inserted 2010.12.30>

Article 6 (Place of Tax Payment)
The place of payment of special rural development tax is the place of payment of the relevant principal tax.
[Wholly amended 2010.12.30]

Article 7 (Returns and Payment)
(1) Special rural development tax under Article 5(1)1 shall be reported and paid together with the relevant principal tax when that principal tax is reported and paid (excluding interim prepayment); where there is no principal tax to report and pay, it shall be reported and paid in accordance with the procedures for reporting and paying the relevant principal tax: Provided, this does not apply where paragraph (3) applies. <Amended 2010.12.30>
(2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), for corporations subject to the consolidated tax payment system under the Corporate Tax Act, the consolidated parent corporation under Article 1(9) of that Act shall report and pay the tax. Article 3(3) of the Corporate Tax Act applies mutatis mutandis to the payment obligation in this case. <Newly inserted 2011.12.31, 2018.12.24>
(3) Where a withholding agent under the Income Tax Act pays income to which Article 5(1)1 or 2 applies, the agent shall collect, report, and pay special rural development tax in accordance with the withholding procedures under the Income Tax Act. <Amended 2010.12.30>
(4) Special rural development tax under Article 5(1)4 through 8 shall be reported and paid together with the relevant principal tax when that principal tax is reported and paid, or collected in transactions (meaning transaction collection under Article 9 of the Securities Transaction Tax Act; the same applies hereinafter) and paid. <Amended 2010.12.30>
(5) Matters necessary for returns, payment, and other matters under paragraphs (1) through (4) shall be prescribed by Presidential Decree. <Amended 2010.12.30, 2011.12.31>
[Title amended 2010.12.30]

Article 8 (Assessment and Collection)
(1) Deleted. <2005.1.5>
(2) Where a person required to report, pay, or withhold special rural development tax under Article 7 fails to file a return, files a return containing errors or omissions, fails to pay the tax payable, or underpays it, the following applies. <Amended 2010.12.30>
1. For taxpayers under Article 3(1) granted reduction of or exemption from income tax or corporate tax, and taxpayers under Article 3(3), (4), and (6) (excluding importers of goods among taxpayers under Article 3(3)), the head of the tax office shall determine, correct, and collect the tax in accordance with the procedures for determining, correcting, and collecting the relevant principal tax;
2. For taxpayers under Article 3(1) granted reduction of or exemption from customs duties and importers of goods among taxpayers under Article 3(3), the head of the customs office shall assess and collect the tax in accordance with the procedures for assessing and collecting customs duties;
3. For taxpayers under Article 3(1) granted reduction of or exemption from acquisition tax or registration and license tax on registration and taxpayers under Article 3(5), the mayor, head of a Gun, or head of an autonomous Gu (hereinafter referred to as "mayor or head of a Gun") shall assess and collect the tax in accordance with the procedures for assessing and collecting the relevant principal tax.
[Title amended 2010.12.30]

Article 9 (Payment in Installments)
(1) Where a taxpayer under a subparagraph of Article 3 pays the principal tax in installments under the relevant tax Act, special rural development tax may also be paid in installments in proportion to the installment amounts, in accordance with the installment procedures for the relevant principal tax.
(2) Even where the principal tax is not paid in installments because it is less than the threshold for installment payment under the relevant tax Act, special rural development tax exceeding 5 million won may be paid in installments as prescribed by Presidential Decree.
[Wholly amended 2010.12.30]

Article 9-2 (Deferral of Payment)
Where a taxpayer under a subparagraph of Article 3 is granted deferral of payment of the principal tax under the relevant tax Act, deferral of payment of special rural development tax may also be granted in accordance with the deferral procedures for that principal tax.
[Article newly inserted 2026.1.27]

Article 10 (Payment into the National Treasury)
When a mayor or head of a Gun collects special rural development tax, the amount shall be paid into the National Treasury as prescribed by Presidential Decree.
[Wholly amended 2010.12.30]

Article 11 (Appeals)
Objections, requests for examination, and requests for adjudication concerning special rural development tax whose principal tax is a local tax shall follow the procedures under the Framework Act on Local Taxes.
[Article newly inserted 2014.1.1]

Article 12 (Refunds)
Refunds of overpaid or erroneously paid special rural development tax and other amounts (including refunds arising from additional collection of tax amounts previously reduced or exempted) shall follow the refund procedures for the principal tax.
[Wholly amended 2010.12.30]

Article 13 (Exclusion from Necessary Expenses or Deductible Expenses)
Special rural development tax on principal tax that is excluded from necessary expenses or deductible expenses under the Income Tax Act or Corporate Tax Act shall be excluded from necessary expenses or deductible expenses in calculating income under the Income Tax Act or Corporate Tax Act.
[Wholly amended 2010.12.30]

ADDENDA <Act No. 4743, 1994.3.24>
Article 1 (Enforcement Date) This Act enters into force on July 1, 1994.
Article 2 (Period of Validity) This Act remains effective until June 30, 2034: Provided, the provisions on special rural development tax under Article 5(1)3 remain effective until December 31, 1996. <Amended 2003.12.31, 2014.1.1, 2023.12.31>
Article 3 (Applicability of Special Rural Development Tax Whose Principal Tax Is Income Tax or Corporate Tax)
(1) Special rural development tax imposed on the amount of income tax or corporate tax reduced or exempted under Article 5(1)1 applies to taxable years ending during the period from the enforcement date of this Act to June 30, 2034 (hereinafter referred to as the "enforcement period"): Provided, reductions or exemptions under Article 15 of the Regulation of Tax Reduction and Exemption Act apply to income arising during the enforcement period of this Act; reductions or exemptions of capital gains tax and special surtax (including corporate tax on gains from transfer) apply to transfers made during the enforcement period. <Amended 2003.12.31, 2014.1.1, 2023.12.31>
(2) Special rural development tax imposed on the amount of income tax reduced or exempted under Article 5(1)2 applies, for reductions or exemptions on interest or dividend income, to income arising during the enforcement period of this Act and, for tax credits, to amounts saved or repaid during the enforcement period.
(3) Special rural development tax under Article 5(1)3 applies from the first day of the business year of a corporation subject to that provision that first ends after the enforcement date of this Act (where a business year ends between July 1, 1994 and December 30, 1994, this means the first day of the business year first beginning after that business year ends), and applies only through business years ending within 2 years.
Article 4 (Applicability of Special Rural Development Tax Whose Principal Tax Is Special Consumption Tax) Special rural development tax whose principal tax is special consumption tax applies to removal, import declaration, or admission during the enforcement period of this Act.
Article 5 (Applicability of Special Rural Development Tax Whose Principal Tax Is Securities Transaction Tax) Special rural development tax whose principal tax is securities transaction tax applies to transfers of share certificates on the stock exchange during the enforcement period of this Act.
Article 6 (Applicability of Special Rural Development Tax Whose Principal Tax Is Customs Duties) Special rural development tax whose principal tax is customs duties applies to import declarations made during the enforcement period of this Act.
Article 7 (Applicability of Special Rural Development Tax Whose Principal Tax Is Local Tax)
(1) Special rural development tax whose principal tax is acquisition tax or registration tax applies to acquisitions, registrations, or recordings during the enforcement period of this Act.
(2) Special rural development tax whose principal tax is aggregate land tax applies where the tax base date falls during the enforcement period of this Act.
(3) Special rural development tax whose principal tax is leisure tax applies to the sale of winning-vote tickets or horse-race betting tickets during the enforcement period of this Act. <Amended 2001.12.29>
Article 8 (Amendment of Other Acts)
(1) The Framework Act on National Taxes is amended as follows.
Item (geo) is newly inserted in Article 2(1) as follows:
(geo) Special rural development tax.
In Article 26-2(1)3, "subparagraphs 1 and 2" is replaced by "subparagraphs 1 through 3"; that subparagraph becomes subparagraph 4 of the same paragraph, and subparagraph 3 is newly inserted in that paragraph as follows:
3. For special rural development tax (excluding tax under Article 5(1)4 of the Act on Special Rural Development Tax), 5 years from the date on which the principal tax under Article 2(2) of the Act on Special Rural Development Tax may be imposed (for special rural development tax imposed on amounts of customs duties reduced or exempted, 2 years, or 5 years where reduction of or exemption from customs duties was obtained by fraud or other improper means).
(2) The Act on Coordination of National Taxes and Local Taxes is amended as follows.
In Article 2, "education tax and transportation tax" is replaced by "education tax, transportation tax, and special rural development tax".
(3) The Regulation of Tax Reduction and Exemption Act is amended as follows.
Subparagraph 13-2 is newly inserted in Article 3(1) as follows:
13-2. Act on Special Rural Development Tax.
(4) The Corporate Tax Act is amended as follows.
Article 22-2(2)1 is replaced as follows:
1. Corporate tax for the relevant business year, special rural development tax imposed on corporate tax reductions or exemptions or on the tax base, and income-based resident tax.
(5) The Value-Added Tax Act is amended as follows.
In Article 13(4), "education tax and transportation tax" is replaced by "education tax, transportation tax, and special rural development tax".
(6) The Customs Act is amended as follows.
In Article 26-2(1), "education tax and transportation tax" is replaced by "education tax, transportation tax, and special rural development tax", and "Education Tax Act and Transportation Tax Act" by "Education Tax Act, Transportation Tax Act, and Act on Special Rural Development Tax".
(7) The Act on Special Cases concerning the Refund of Customs Duties and Other Taxes on Raw Materials for Export is amended as follows.
In Article 1, "liquor tax and transportation tax" is replaced by "liquor tax, transportation tax, and special rural development tax", and "Liquor Tax Act and Transportation Tax Act" by "Liquor Tax Act, Transportation Tax Act, and Act on Special Rural Development Tax".
In Article 2(1), "liquor tax and transportation tax" is replaced by "liquor tax, transportation tax, and special rural development tax".

